# ⛔ .env is ignored above, but .env.bak.* was NOT -- and two such files sat
# here holding 3 populated secrets, one "git add -A" away from GitHub. The
# habit that protects a file (take a backup first) is the habit that exposed
# it. Backups belong in /root/edit-backups, never beside the original; these
# patterns are the second line of defence for when someone forgets.
*.bak
*.bak.*
.env.*.bak
.env.preSymlink.bak
*.orig
*.save
